    "['local-address [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 100', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\n neighbor vpnv4 update-source Loopback0\\n##\\n\\nNote: This assumes that Loopback0 on the Cisco device is configured with the IP address 3.3.3.9/32, similar to the Juniper configuration where lo0.0 has address 3.3.3.9/32. The Cisco command uses the loopback interface as the source for BGP sessions rather than explicitly specifying the IP address.\", 'trans_template': 'router bgp 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor vpnv4 update-source Loopback0', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\n neighbor vpnv4 update-source Loopback0\\n##\\n\\nNote: This assumes that Loopback0 on the Cisco device is configured with the IP address 3.3.3.9/32, similar to the Juniper configuration where lo0.0 has address 3.3.3.9/32. The Cisco command uses the loopback interface as the source for BGP sessions rather than explicitly specifying the IP address.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor vpnv4 update-source Loopback0'}]]": 1,
