    "['neighbor [parameter2] family [parameter3] [parameter4]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 100', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper BGP configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\n neighbor 1.1.1.9 address-family vpnv4 unicast\\n##\\n\\nThe Cisco command:\\n1. Begins with the BGP AS number (100, from the peer-as setting)\\n2. Specifies the same neighbor IP (1.1.1.9)\\n3. Uses \"vpnv4\" address family which is Cisco\\'s equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"inet-vpn\"\\n4. Maintains the unicast specification\\n5. In Cisco, this would be part of the BGP router configuration context', 'trans_template': 'router bgp 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 1.1.1.9 address-family vpnv4 unicast', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper BGP configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\n neighbor 1.1.1.9 address-family vpnv4 unicast\\n##\\n\\nThe Cisco command:\\n1. Begins with the BGP AS number (100, from the peer-as setting)\\n2. Specifies the same neighbor IP (1.1.1.9)\\n3. Uses \"vpnv4\" address family which is Cisco\\'s equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"inet-vpn\"\\n4. Maintains the unicast specification\\n5. In Cisco, this would be part of the BGP router configuration context', 'trans_template': 'neighbor 1.1.1.9 address-family vpnv4 unicast'}]]": 1,
    "['neighbor [parameter2] family [parameter3] [parameter4]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 1.1.1.9 send-community both', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper BGP L2VPN signaling configuration:\\n\\n##\\nneighbor 1.1.1.9 send-community both\\nneighbor 1.1.1.9 address-family l2vpn vpls\\n##\\n\\nThe Cisco configuration requires two commands to achieve the equivalent functionality:\\n1. First enables sending of BGP communities to the neighbor\\n2. Second activates the L2VPN VPLS address family for that neighbor, which handles the signaling equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"family l2vpn signaling\"', 'trans_template': 'neighbor 1.1.1.9 send-community both'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 1.1.1.9 address-family l2vpn vpls', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper BGP L2VPN signaling configuration:\\n\\n##\\nneighbor 1.1.1.9 send-community both\\nneighbor 1.1.1.9 address-family l2vpn vpls\\n##\\n\\nThe Cisco configuration requires two commands to achieve the equivalent functionality:\\n1. First enables sending of BGP communities to the neighbor\\n2. Second activates the L2VPN VPLS address family for that neighbor, which handles the signaling equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"family l2vpn signaling\"', 'trans_template': 'neighbor 1.1.1.9 address-family l2vpn vpls'}]]": 1,
